{
 "mutations": [
  {
   "patch": {
    "id": "post-statement-of-account",
    "ifRevisionID": "zqObMY4AZ2PLBMUzA5y1CY",
    "set": {
     "title": "How to Make a Billing Statement (Statement of Account), With a Worked Sample",
     "seoTitle": "How to Make a Billing Statement: Steps, Sample and Aging",
     "seoDescription": "How to make a billing statement, also called a statement of account: what goes on it, how it differs from an invoice, and a worked sample with aging columns.",
     "excerpt": "A billing statement, or statement of account, sums up every invoice, payment and credit on a customer's account for a period and shows what is still owed. Here is how to make one, how aging columns work, and a sample that reconciles to the cent.",
     "body": [
      {
       "_key": "4daedcdd2296",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "45f95f3e05d7",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [
          "strong"
         ],
         "text": "To make a billing statement, also called a statement of account, list every invoice, payment and credit on one customer's account for a period, usually a month. Start from the opening balance, keep a running balance on each line, and end with the total still owed, how much of it is overdue, and how to pay. Unlike an invoice, a statement does not bill anything new; it shows where the account stands."
        },
        {
         "_key": "c37b8a530624",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": " Customers who buy on credit often pay from the statement rather than from each invoice."
        }
       ],
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "normal"
      },
      {
       "_key": "ed8a97775bc6",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "ef847936a048",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": "Each line on a statement points back to an invoice, so the invoices come first. Our "
        },
        {
         "_key": "a0a836c31bf9",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [
          "e2ea10e5fe9f"
         ],
         "text": "invoice template"
        },
        {
         "_key": "bd26306dcc45",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": " handles those, and a clean numbering system, covered in "
        },
        {
         "_key": "31ba46004e41",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [
          "74babacd0d97"
         ],
         "text": "how to number invoices"
        },
        {
         "_key": "44ed414b80ac",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": ", is what lets a customer tick each statement line off against their own records."
        }
       ],
       "markDefs": [
        {
         "_key": "e2ea10e5fe9f",
         "_type": "link",
         "href": "/templates/invoice"
        },
        {
         "_key": "74babacd0d97",
         "_type": "link",
         "href": "/blog/invoice-number"
        }
       ],
       "style": "normal"
      },
      {
       "_key": "ebdb46c5aa6a",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "2420d7e9897f",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": "Billing Statement vs. Invoice"
        }
       ],
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "h2"
      },
      {
       "_key": "7abd68b271fa",
       "_type": "table",
       "rows": [
        {
         "_key": "0f02b4d4abf2",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "",
          "Invoice",
          "Billing statement"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "7c2f1b0f7c1f",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Covers",
          "One sale or job",
          "Every transaction in a period"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "09f8ebfa6c1f",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Asks for payment?",
          "Yes, for that sale",
          "Shows the total balance and what is overdue"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "27f18eada44b",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Shows payments and credits?",
          "Rarely",
          "Yes, all of them"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "ca31c03805a4",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Frequency",
          "Each time you bill",
          "Usually monthly"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "f2b16cb5f876",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Main number",
          "Invoice number",
          "Statement date and account number"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "fdf2cad9224c",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Who needs it",
          "Every customer you bill",
          "Customers on account (regular credit buyers)"
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "_key": "1e6ffaba2734",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "acf9a3853dd2",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": "If a customer pays every invoice on the spot, a statement adds little. It earns its place when one customer has several open invoices, partial payments and credits at once."
        }
       ],
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "normal"
      },
      {
       "_key": "6b95e861c387",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "72ca2cf70d0d",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": "What Goes on a Billing Statement"
        }
       ],
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "h2"
      },
      {
       "_key": "3f97dde8ec6a",
       "_type": "table",
       "rows": [
        {
         "_key": "41061f83c83c",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Section",
          "What to include"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "9d342c931a4b",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Header",
          "Your business details, a heading such as STATEMENT or STATEMENT OF ACCOUNT, statement date"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "432b09a7e28d",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Customer",
          "Name, address, account number"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "bdf226f028fd",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Period",
          "e.g. Nov 1 to Nov 30, 2026"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "d05a08816045",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Opening balance",
          "What was owed at the start of the period"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "28e6472fa7b7",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Transactions",
          "Date, reference (invoice, payment, credit memo), charge, credit, running balance"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "934b2dbc2e5d",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Closing balance",
          "Total owed at the statement date"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "c9755b96e470",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Aging summary",
          "How much of the balance is current and how much is overdue, by age"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "e8c07a500e57",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Payment details",
          "How to pay and whom to call with a query"
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "_key": "16446e63a03c",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "de9b0d814d24",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": "How Aging Columns Work"
        }
       ],
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "h2"
      },
      {
       "_key": "82c2788b6dec",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "fe2efa01fb73",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": "An aging summary splits the closing balance by how long each amount has been past its due date. The usual buckets are:"
        }
       ],
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "normal"
      },
      {
       "_key": "3ac436f4fb01",
       "_type": "table",
       "rows": [
        {
         "_key": "f0c539b9074c",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Bucket",
          "Meaning"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "c58b5869165a",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Current",
          "Not yet due"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "55778a32b268",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "1\u201330 days",
          "Up to 30 days past the due date"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "c378cee75e56",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "31\u201360 days",
          "31 to 60 days past due"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "7d612399a634",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "61\u201390 days",
          "61 to 90 days past due"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "0e9e1b88b2a9",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Over 90 days",
          "More than 90 days past due"
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "_key": "f09060ab81fd",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "c81207f9baa3",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": "Two rules keep it accurate. Age each invoice from its "
        },
        {
         "_key": "5f381f42712d",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [
          "strong"
         ],
         "text": "due date"
        },
        {
         "_key": "f8b61373c8e7",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": ", not its issue date. And apply payments to the "
        },
        {
         "_key": "7ac01ffc0676",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [
          "strong"
         ],
         "text": "oldest invoice first"
        },
        {
         "_key": "ec8efe458a39",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": " unless the customer says which invoice they are paying; a payment marked for a specific invoice goes against that one."
        }
       ],
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "normal"
      },
      {
       "_key": "9a12a1beea0c",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "8db3bdef2e99",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": "How to Make a Billing Statement, Step by Step"
        }
       ],
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "h2"
      },
      {
       "_key": "53369449a0c9",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "e7d832f20561",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [
          "strong"
         ],
         "text": "Choose the period"
        },
        {
         "_key": "3652fbe5dcfc",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": ", usually the calendar month."
        }
       ],
       "level": 1,
       "listItem": "number",
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "normal"
      },
      {
       "_key": "71bbd52cedc8",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "32ebdcb5ff7c",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [
          "strong"
         ],
         "text": "Carry forward the opening balance"
        },
        {
         "_key": "04c4720bdf34",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": " from last month's closing balance."
        }
       ],
       "level": 1,
       "listItem": "number",
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "normal"
      },
      {
       "_key": "dec6f7791165",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "63798bac36a4",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [
          "strong"
         ],
         "text": "List every transaction in date order"
        },
        {
         "_key": "89f6467f98b9",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": ": invoices as charges, payments and credit memos as credits."
        }
       ],
       "level": 1,
       "listItem": "number",
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "normal"
      },
      {
       "_key": "73747be53cc6",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "d509e3e57ff2",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [
          "strong"
         ],
         "text": "Keep a running balance"
        },
        {
         "_key": "6a4d12250195",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": " on every line."
        }
       ],
       "level": 1,
       "listItem": "number",
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "normal"
      },
      {
       "_key": "fa56838cd426",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "5a320cbc3f71",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [
          "strong"
         ],
         "text": "Check the closing balance"
        },
        {
         "_key": "7eed21edab51",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": " against the open invoices in your records. They must agree."
        }
       ],
       "level": 1,
       "listItem": "number",
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "normal"
      },
      {
       "_key": "f54ad7cba820",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "ba1e84d79a48",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [
          "strong"
         ],
         "text": "Age what is still open"
        },
        {
         "_key": "8c46ea6792e4",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": " into the buckets above."
        }
       ],
       "level": 1,
       "listItem": "number",
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "normal"
      },
      {
       "_key": "4920c61df1f2",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "d81040597618",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [
          "strong"
         ],
         "text": "Send it"
        },
        {
         "_key": "fc39ee7364cf",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": " a day or two after the period ends, with payment details at the bottom."
        }
       ],
       "level": 1,
       "listItem": "number",
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "normal"
      },
      {
       "_key": "da880b7471e1",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "2b37ccfa13f4",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": "A Worked Example"
        }
       ],
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "h2"
      },
      {
       "_key": "beecf04f8aa3",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "632a4581137e",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": "Sample data: a fictional linen service and a fictional restaurant customer on Net 30 terms."
        }
       ],
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "normal"
      },
      {
       "_key": "0d0523c2086a",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "a3ef122cbb50",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [
          "strong"
         ],
         "text": "STATEMENT OF ACCOUNT"
        },
        {
         "_key": "d1c609a60840",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": " \u00b7 Statement date: Nov 30, 2026"
        }
       ],
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "blockquote"
      },
      {
       "_key": "a27b7df64b5c",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "393078c43482",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [
          "strong"
         ],
         "text": "From:"
        },
        {
         "_key": "edbd1f5a5670",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": " Harbor Linen Service, 52 Wharf St, Charleston, SC 29401"
        }
       ],
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "blockquote"
      },
      {
       "_key": "83833df8af78",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "ebbe2fa328c1",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [
          "strong"
         ],
         "text": "To:"
        },
        {
         "_key": "61fe4d26d757",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": " Bayside Bistro, 9 Marina Way, Charleston, SC 29412 \u00b7 Account BB-207"
        }
       ],
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "blockquote"
      },
      {
       "_key": "5ba9c50ca1d7",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "b644578c8fd0",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [
          "strong"
         ],
         "text": "Period:"
        },
        {
         "_key": "563803bd4e90",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": " Nov 1 to Nov 30, 2026"
        }
       ],
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "blockquote"
      },
      {
       "_key": "64db807bc7eb",
       "_type": "table",
       "rows": [
        {
         "_key": "5b944dad1786",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Date",
          "Reference",
          "Charges",
          "Credits",
          "Balance"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "7303048f360f",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Nov 1",
          "Balance forward (INV-3301, Oct 15)",
          "",
          "",
          "$640.00"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "b2845d37e5d1",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Nov 3",
          "Payment received, thank you",
          "",
          "$400.00",
          "$240.00"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "566f40b05155",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Nov 7",
          "INV-3342",
          "$520.00",
          "",
          "$760.00"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "1d36615fbce4",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Nov 14",
          "INV-3360",
          "$480.00",
          "",
          "$1,240.00"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "6ccdaf047d89",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Nov 20",
          "Credit memo CM-0042 (stained napkins, INV-3360)",
          "",
          "$60.00",
          "$1,180.00"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "11fbb6eff13f",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Nov 28",
          "INV-3377",
          "$505.00",
          "",
          "$1,685.00"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "babfb996b31c",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "",
          "**Balance due**",
          "",
          "",
          "**$1,685.00**"
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "_key": "e6fd1b158220",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "a70cf878f5f9",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": "The $400 payment went against the oldest invoice, INV-3301, leaving $240 open on it. That invoice was due Nov 14, so on Nov 30 it is 16 days late. Everything else is not yet due."
        }
       ],
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "normal"
      },
      {
       "_key": "7bdfe69221c9",
       "_type": "table",
       "rows": [
        {
         "_key": "b37bf669a9e7",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "Current",
          "1\u201330 days",
          "31\u201360 days",
          "61\u201390 days",
          "Over 90",
          "Total"
         ]
        },
        {
         "_key": "73e697ea8365",
         "_type": "tableRow",
         "cells": [
          "$1,445.00",
          "$240.00",
          "$0.00",
          "$0.00",
          "$0.00",
          "$1,685.00"
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "_key": "abc97a3bcd4c",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "ab7230dc9bf7",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": "The current column is INV-3342 ($520.00), INV-3360 after its credit ($420.00) and INV-3377 ($505.00), which add to $1,445.00. With the $240.00 overdue, that matches the $1,685.00 balance. If the columns do not add to the balance, something is missing from the list. Credits like the one on Nov 20 are explained in our guide to the "
        },
        {
         "_key": "931450574c30",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [
          "2fb600eb8ff0"
         ],
         "text": "credit memo"
        },
        {
         "_key": "26fd17d9ce49",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": "."
        }
       ],
       "markDefs": [
        {
         "_key": "2fb600eb8ff0",
         "_type": "link",
         "href": "/blog/credit-memo"
        }
       ],
       "style": "normal"
      },
      {
       "_key": "41e0e0aeda0d",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "765874bb251c",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": "What a Customer Does With It"
        }
       ],
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "h2"
      },
      {
       "_key": "3d33927240cd",
       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "a2d76c202f2f",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": "A good statement lets the customer's bookkeeper do three things quickly: match each invoice to their own records, spot anything they have not received, and pay the overdue amount first. In the sample, Bayside Bistro would pay the $240.00 now and the rest by each invoice's due date."
        }
       ],
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "normal"
      },
      {
       "_key": "a0b50768eaba",
       "_type": "block",
       "style": "h2",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "0e8c4a621088",
         "_type": "span",
         "text": "What If the Customer Paid Only Part?",
         "marks": []
        }
       ],
       "markDefs": []
      },
      {
       "_key": "b0c3fe6dfb7e",
       "_type": "block",
       "style": "normal",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "1131f96f9466",
         "_type": "span",
         "text": "Show the partial payment as its own line and let the running balance carry the rest forward, as the $400 payment does in the sample. Note which invoice it went against. If the customer wants proof of that payment on its own, send a receipt for it; our guide to the ",
         "marks": []
        },
        {
         "_key": "7c9b31644b80",
         "_type": "span",
         "text": "partial payment receipt",
         "marks": [
          "4a701791f5c9"
         ]
        },
        {
