       "_type": "block",
       "children": [
        {
         "_key": "77f899cefd7f",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": "A statement is a summary, not a source document. The records behind it are the invoices, payment records and credit memos, and those are what the IRS lists among the "
        },
        {
         "_key": "1e1951a9c594",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [
          "33db426571d6"
         ],
         "text": "supporting documents for gross receipts"
        },
        {
         "_key": "318a0647b79a",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": ". Keep them filed by customer and number so any statement line can be traced back. This is general information, not tax or accounting advice."
        }
       ],
       "markDefs": [
        {
         "_key": "33db426571d6",
         "_type": "link",
         "href": "https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/what-kind-of-records-should-i-keep"
