        {
         "_key": "1e9134ba684b",
         "_type": "span",
         "marks": [],
         "text": "A statement should list only real invoices, payments and credits on the customer's account."
        }
       ],
       "markDefs": [],
       "style": "normal"
      }
     ],
     "faqs": [
      {
       "_key": "8095ed42ca98",
       "_type": "object",
       "answer": "A summary a business sends a customer, usually monthly, listing every invoice, payment and credit for the period with a running balance and the total still owed. It is also called a statement of account or customer statement.",
       "question": "What is a billing statement?"
      },
      {
       "_key": "846710b9a784",
       "_type": "object",
       "answer": "No. An invoice bills one sale. A statement summarizes all of a customer's invoices, payments and credits over a period and shows the overall balance and what is overdue.",
       "question": "Is a billing statement the same as an invoice?"
      },
      {
       "_key": "d40a228341b1",
       "_type": "object",
       "question": "Is a billing statement the same as a bill?",
       "answer": "In everyday speech people call both a bill. Strictly, the invoice is the bill for one sale, and the statement summarizes the account, which may include several bills."
      },
      {
       "_key": "91920a6b978f",
       "_type": "object",
       "answer": "They split the balance by how long each amount has been past its due date, typically Current, 1\u201330, 31\u201360, 61\u201390 and over 90 days. They show the customer what to pay first.",
